{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43698 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is implicated in the interaction with SNU1 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of cellular processes. The evidence suggests that Fluoranthene acts as a target for Ataxin-2, a protein that is itself a target of multiple compounds, including Yuanhunine and (-)-Duryne F. These compounds, in turn, target SNU1, indicating a potential pathway where Fluoranthene may influence SNU1 through these intermediaries. The shared involvement of Ataxin-2 as a target across different compounds highlights a possible functional overlap, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways suggests that Fluoranthene may exert its effects on SNU1 via a complex network of molecular targets, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise nature of this relationship.",
